# Demo app: operations and your access

Written by Aurora from the app's catalogue and your grants. The gateway decides every request;
workspace and organization policy can be stricter than this list, never looser.

## Accounts
- A: `c_1` Label c_1 (full access)

## Webhook: Ops alerts (account A, `send_ops_alerts`)

Deploy results.

| slot | type | required | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `text` | string | yes | The message; at most 200 characters |
| `level` | enum | no | one of info, warn |
| `count` | integer | no |  |
| `ratio` | number | no |  |
| `urgent` | boolean | no |  |
| `tags` | string list | no | at most 20 characters; at most 5 items |
| `card` | json | no |  |

```
curl -sS -X POST https://c_1.link.aurora.internal/ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"text":"…"}'
```
Add `-H 'X-Aurora-Dry-Run: 1'` to check the body without sending.

## Read
- `list_things` GET /v1/things: List things. All things. [allowed]
- `get_thing` GET /v1/things/*: Get a thing. [allowed]

## Write
- `make_thing` POST /v1/things: Make a thing. [allowed]

## Requests that match no operation above
[allowed]
